WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.157
Use this guide to decide what kind of action the evidence supports.

00:00:04.157 --> 00:00:07.847
A known formatting difference can be standardized.

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:13.112
A documented blank-as-missing convention can be normalized.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:18.467
An invalid value with unknown truth should be flagged or quarantined.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:23.082
Possible duplicates need detection and resolution logic.

00:00:23.082 --> 00:00:26.342
A supported correction can be applied safely.

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:30.697
And stable rules can become constraints for future prevention.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:38.372
Connect this idea to a healthcare pipeline validating contact, demographic, and event fields.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:44.117
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:51.457
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:51.457 --> 00:00:57.637
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:57.637 --> 00:01:04.000
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
